# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what the image needs.
# Anything new (.env, .git, notes, images, venvs) stays out of the build context by
# default, so secrets and junk cannot leak into an image by accident.
*

!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!pytest.ini
!backend/
# Person B's graph package; silently absent until it exists.
!agent/

# Re-exclude junk inside the allowed directories.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Docs are not needed at runtime (and editing a README should not rebuild the image).
**/*.md
